en:
Experienced workers propose improvements for their machine and part:
• a fixture: the operation is 12% faster;
• an inspection gauge: 20% fewer rejects for the part;
• machine care: wear is 25% slower.
Implement it and pay the author, or reject it. With “Socialist competition” proposals come twice as often.

A radio room and loudspeakers under the ceiling:
• 8:15, morning plant news;
• 10:00, workplace exercises, people tire less;
• music at lunch, lunch is more fun.

The music follows the situation; each time of day has several pieces of its own:
• morning (6–10 h): “First Shift”, “Path to the Gatehouse”, “Morning Bus”;
• day: “The Quota”, “Avenue Lights”, “Second-Floor Buffet”, “Foundry”, “Quiet Shop”;
• rush (less than 30 hours to an order's deadline): “Counter-Plan”, “Shock Shift”, “Foundry”;
• evening (18–22 h): “Shift Change”, “Over the Factory River”, “Factory Waltz”, “Second-Floor Buffet”;
• night: “Night Shift”, “Night Broadcast”, “Quiet Shop”.
In winter “First Snow” plays first, in the rain “Rain on the Shop Roof”. In the main menu, “The Gatehouse”.
A track doesn't cut off: it plays to the end of the musical phrase and flows smoothly into the next; the same piece never plays twice in a row. Under the pause menu the music is quieter. The mode is “Music selection” in settings.
